# Requests against a locally started order service (README, quick start).
# IntelliJ IDEA runs them with the built-in HTTP Client; the handler scripts keep the id of the created order.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Create an order
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: checkout-1

{
  "customerId": 1001,
  "items": [
    {"productId": "sku-1", "quantity": 2, "price": 10.50},
    {"productId": "sku-2", "quantity": 1, "price": 5.25}
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### Read the order back
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### Cancel it - publishes order-cancelled
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
X-Correlation-Id: checkout-1-cancel

### Cancel it again - 409, nothing is published
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel

### An unknown order - 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/999999

### An invalid order - 400 naming every rejected field
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 0,
  "items": [
    {"productId": "", "quantity": 0, "price": 10.505}
  ]
}

### The OpenAPI document (Swagger UI: {{host}}/swagger-ui.html)
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs

### Outbox DLQ - how many events are waiting there
GET {{host}}/api/outbox-dlq/events/count?status=MOVED

### Outbox DLQ - one event, by the id from the count or the logs
@dlqEventId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
GET {{host}}/api/outbox-dlq/events/{{dlqEventId}}

### Outbox DLQ - send the event back to the outbox for another round of retries
PATCH {{host}}/api/outbox-dlq/events/{{dlqEventId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"status": "TO_RETRY"}

### Health
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
